Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-27-2000||08:19 AM||||There's a ad in a local newspaper for a Fiero GTU...   What is a GTU??  Is there such a thing??  the ad has no phone # and only a address ....  only 300 miles from me.. so i'm not stopping by on my way home from work though.....   anyone have a clue WHEN a GTU was made???    steve||||reg||3
Z||000001||Carrolles||09-27-2000||08:59 AM||||As far as I know Pontiac never made a GTU.  Perhaps the ad is referring to a GT or it has aftermarket GTU style body panels.<P>I find that many car ads for Fieros are loaded with mistakes like Power Steering, 4 spd auto, 2+2, etc.  I even saw one in AutoTrader with a picture of a typical Fiero Coupe listing it as a 4 door.  These are usually run by car dealers that write up the usual stuff on all their cars but don't pay particular attention to what they actually have.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||HugGRRRFiero||09-27-2000||09:09 AM||||Yep, with the IMSA type fender flares.  Pontiac never made a production GTU, but they did make some road racing cars (maybe 1/4 actual stock Fiero parts in them), doubt very much tho that is one of those.  Likely it's a GT and the guy selling it don't know.  He's probably still looking for the engine under the hood.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>GTU - Grand Turismo Uglymagato?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">        <BR>        <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-27-2000||05:25 PM||||hhmmmm.....  I remember another place that I saw a GTU...  In the Fiero Store's catalog on page# 1 (inside of front cover) at the bottom of the page...  look at the black Fiero manual..  I'll pause this for a minute so that everyone can go get there catalog from the Fiero Store.................................................................  OK  I'm back now and hope that all has returned with the catalog....  If you can read the 1st line of it it say's....<BR>     2m4--Turbo--GT--GTU--Fomula<P>What's that turbo sh*t also??  <BR>anyone have a clue ??   thank's Steve||||reg||1
Z||000004||DjKid||09-27-2000||05:56 PM||||I dont wanna sound prodealer.. or try to make them sound smart.. hehe.. cuz my personal experince was that they dont know where a fiero's engine is!! but.. umm... my engine is under my hood. hehe.. also called a rear decklid.  hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> that thing up front I call a sparetire holder<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe<BR><A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||sombre||09-27-2000||07:33 PM||||<BR>    Look a little closer at the cover of that book and you'll find that it is a copy of Brooklands' fiero....It's a collection of reprint magazine articles from back in the 80's about the fiero.Brooklands does this for many cars.I have the book also have one for gen 3 camaros and gen 3 firebirds.<P>   The turbo refers to a test article from an aftermarket company for a turbo kit for the iron duke.<P>  The GTU is the road race version of the fiero.Not much in common with the street car other than name and drive/engine configuration.This is the car that got the famed SD-4 engine.<P>  I'd guess the add is a typo or that someone bought the panels and put them on a street car.I think IRM still sells them.<P>                          Greg<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-27-2000||10:39 PM||||Ok ... I see...   Thank's for clearing this all up for me....   Steve||||reg||1
